ANSWER OF NORTHERN VIRGINIA ELECTRIC COOPERATIVE, INC. AND 
NORTHEASTERN RURAL ELECTRIC MEMBERSHIP CORPORATION OPPOSING 
THE JOINT COMMENTS AND MOTION TO STAY PROCEEDINGS AND REQUEST 
TO ESTABLISH SETTLEMENT JUDGE PROCEDURES 

Pursuant to Rule 213 of the Rules of Practice and Procedure of the Federal Energy 
Regulatory Commission (“FERC” or the “Commission”),1 Northern Virginia Electric 
Cooperative, Inc. (“NOVEC”) and Northeastern Rural Electric Membership Corporation 
(“NREMC”) respectfully submit this answer in opposition to the Joint Parties’ April 22, 2025, 
“Joint Comments and Motion to Stay Proceedings and Request to Establish Settlement Judge 
Procedures” (“Motion”).2 

1 18 C.F.R. § 385.213.  
2 Joint Parties, Joint Comments and Motion to Stay Proceedings and Request to Establish Settlement Judge Procedures, 
Docket Nos. EL25-49-000, et al. (filed April 22, 2025) (Accession No. 20250422-5166) (“Motion”). The Joint Parties 
are a group of generators and trade associations that includes the Electric Power Supply Association, the PJM Power 
Providers Group, Calpine Corporation, Cogentrix Energy Power Management, LLC, Constellation Energy 
Generation, LLC, and LS Power Development, LLC.
